(text "CoCo 3 2 MB SRAM expansion - memory board (plugs into CN4/CN5/CN6)" (at 25.40 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid c13911ea-66ab-40d4-9db6-b29490b3fdfd))
(text "Remove IC16-IC19 and cut C65, C66 first (as for any 512K upgrade)." (at 25.40 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid bdb591e6-2bdc-4ad5-9844-85854a80eae7))
(text "J3 takes BANK0/BANK1 (physical A19/A20) from the DAT board. Unconnected: R1/R2 pull low = 512K mode." (at 25.40 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 8b4c2e43-cc46-4adb-be66-4e6e4e72a83e))
(text "Write logic (active low): ~BHE = ~WE0 XOR 1   ~BLE = ~WE1 XOR 1   ~WE = ~WE1 XOR ~BHE" (at 160.02 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid d14f4e1a-c613-4bb4-bb46-9be10a7004e0))
(text "RAS = ~RAS XOR 1 clocks U3/U4: row address (9 bits) and BANK1:0 latched on the falling edge of ~RAS." (at 160.02 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 481045bd-e686-4094-96fa-0e09c4a0ed26))
(text "SRAM ~CE1 = ~CAS, CE2 = BYTE = 1 (x16), ~OE = 0. Address/data pin order is permuted for routing." (at 160.02 40.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 360b3c62-4f1e-4ebe-b1e4-581cdad87321))
(text "Derived from cc3-512k by Ciaran Anscomb (CC BY-SA 4.0), logic per Jim Brain. This design is CC BY-SA 4.0." (at 25.40 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 8481f3b6-6b98-4e5f-ae8d-fd3a30cfa124))
